# NOTICE

This product includes code and detection patterns adapted from the following
MIT-licensed project:

- **ai-job-search** - https://github.com/ai-job-search-dev/ai-job-search
  Copyright (c) 2026 Mads Lorentzen

Behavior-level adoptions (reference concepts made concrete in my engine):
- ATS deal-breakers (`agent/ats.py`): hard-requirement terms the posting
  names (visa, sponsorship, security clearance) and the resume does not
  address are surfaced in the ATS report as an advisory gap, never vetoing
  a run - the user decides what "requires" means.

Adapted in this repository:

- `agent/posting_guard.py` - posting integrity gate (hidden-HTML removal,
  invisible-Unicode cleaning, instruction-shaped-line detection). Adapted
  from `tools/posting_guard.py`; adopted the reference's shell/config
  instruction patterns (`curl|wget|ssh|scp`, `.env`, `settings.json`,
  `allowed-tools`) as extras (they were the one pattern gap).
- `agent/pdf_verify.py` - shipped-PDF text-layer verification (text layer,
  CID/replacement damage, ASCII date separators, required literals).
  Adapted from `tools/verify_pdf.py` and the ASCII-date rule in
  `.claude/skills/job-application-assistant/05-cv-templates.md`.
- `agent/robots_check.py` - RFC 9309 robots.txt gate for job-posting fetches
  (longest-match, BOM, decodable-rule checks; the spec's cautious fail-closed
  rules; the GHSA-xhqf-8q8x-4jwm backtracking regression is pinned). Adapted
  from `tools/robots_check.py`; the browser-header retry lives in
  `agent/url_fetch.py` per its robots gate.
- `agent/verify_layout.py` - compiled-PDF layout measurement (holes,
  orphaned entry headers across page breaks, footer collisions, thin final
  page, early page ends). Adapted from `tools/verify_layout.py`.
- `agent/trim.py` - relevance-weighted trim suggestions (posting relevance,
  uniqueness, cover-letter narrative load). Adapted from the
  "Relevance-weighted cutting" guidance in
  `.claude/skills/job-application-assistant/05-cv-templates.md`.

